    SHORT REPORT
    
    Adenine methylation is very scarce in the
    Drosophila genome and not erased by
    the ten-­eleven translocation dioxygenase
    Manon Boulet1†, Guerric Gilbert1†, Yoan Renaud1†, Martina Schmidt-­Dengler2,
    Emilie Plantié1, Romane Bertrand1, Xinsheng Nan3, Tomasz Jurkowski3,
    Mark Helm2, Laurence Vandel1*, Lucas Waltzer1*
    1
    
    Université Clermont Auvergne, CNRS, INSERM, iGReD, Clermont-­Ferrand, France;
